<title>UK: U.K. 4th Qtr cocoa grind fell 3.3 PCT on year.</title>
<headline>U.K. 4th Qtr cocoa grind fell 3.3 PCT on year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.K. 4th quarter 1996 cocoa grind fell 3.3 percent to 45,147 tonnes when compared with 46,688 in the same period in 1995, the Biscuit, Cake, Chocolate and Confectionery Alliance (BCCCA) said.</p>
<p>The result compares with expectations the grind would fall by up to ten percent in the quarter from the year before. London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
</text>
